hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1237","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Keep your children close to you until the early part of the evening passes. That is the time when the devils spread out.\"""""
"1238","'Say farewell to Salma if you prepare to go in the morning,\n White hair and Islam is enough prohibition for a man'\n\n'Umar said, 'Enough! You have spoken the truth. You have spoken the truth.'\""1239"""
"1239","Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, saying: Ma'mar informed us, from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jahshi, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, who said: Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) would pass by us at midday or close to it, and say: ""Stand up and take a midday nap (qaylulah), for what remains is for the devil."""
"1240","Anas said, \At the time that wine was made unlawful"
"1241","Here is the translated text in English:

Musa narrated to us, saying: Sulaiman bin al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, who said: I, Anas, said: The people of Medina did not have a drink, after the prohibition of wine, as astonishing as the date and the grape. So, I would pour the drink for the companions of the Messenger of Allah, and they were at Abu Talhah's. A man got up and said: Wine has been prohibited. What did they say? ""When?"" or ""Until we see?"" They said: ""O Anas, pour it out!"" Then they went to Umm Sulaim's, until they had washed and purified themselves, and then Umm Sulaim poured water over them, and then they went to the Prophet, and the report was as the man had said. I, Anas, said: What did they eat after that?"
"1242","Khawwat ibn Jubayr said, \Sleep at the beginning of the day is stupidity"
